#: simple-custom-post-order.php:2244
msgid "Show this drag handle when hovering a row"
msgstr ""

#: simple-custom-post-order.php:2247
msgid ""
"Rows stay draggable from anywhere — this just adds the grip icon as a hover "
"cue. Keyboard users can always reveal the handle by tabbing to a row, so "
"turning this off does not affect accessibility. Applies to the Modern "
"engine."
msgstr ""

#: simple-custom-post-order.php:2257
msgid "Configure advanced plugin options."
msgstr ""

#: simple-custom-post-order.php:2272
msgid "Show all registered post types (including hidden ones)"
msgstr ""

#: simple-custom-post-order.php:2274
msgid ""
"Enable this to see post types that are normally hidden from the admin menu. "
"For advanced users only."
msgstr ""

#: simple-custom-post-order.php:2289
msgid "Let me change an item’s parent by dragging it sideways"
msgstr ""

#: simple-custom-post-order.php:2291
msgid ""
"On hierarchical post types (such as Pages) and taxonomies (such as "
"Categories), drag a row to the right to nest it under the item above, or to "
"the left to move it back out — the dashes in front of the title show where "
"it will land. With the keyboard, grab a row and press the Right or Left "
"arrow key. Moving a published page under another page changes its address "
"(URL), and WordPress does not redirect the old address, so update any links "
"to it. Off by default. Applies to the Modern engine. Developers can "
"override with the scpo_allow_reparent filter."
msgstr ""

